    {
      "text": "Word … dwelt among us, John 1:14. Rabbi … where dwellest thou, John 1:38. drinketh my blood, dwelleth in me, John 6:56. Father that dwelleth in me, John 14:10. most High dwelleth not in temples made with hands, Acts 7:48 (17:24). Paul dwelt two whole years in his own hired house, Acts 28:30. in me … dwelleth no good thing, Rom. 7:18. Spirit of God dwell in you, Rom. 8:9 (1 Cor. 3:16). God hath said, I will dwell in them, 2 Cor. 6:16. Christ may dwell in your hearts, Eph. 3:17. in him should all fulness dwell, Col. 1:19. in him dwelleth all the fulness of the Godhead, Col. 2:9. Let the word of Christ dwell in you richly, Col. 3:16. dwelling in the light which no man can approach, 1 Tim. 6:16. Holy Ghost which dwelleth in us, 2 Tim. 1:14. he that keepeth his commandments dwelleth in him, 1 Jn. 3:24. If we love one another, God dwelleth in us, 1 Jn. 4:12. know we that we dwell in him, 1 Jn. 4:13. he that dwelleth in love dwelleth in God, 1 Jn. 4:16. sitteth on the throne shall dwell among them, Rev. 7:15. he will dwell with them, Rev. 21:3.",
